    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "5 Australian Broadcasting Corporation",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983#sec-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983.pdf, p.12",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The body corporate that was, immediately before the commencing\nday, in existence by virtue of section 30 of the Broadcasting and\nTelevision Act 1942 under the name Australian Broadcasting\nCommission continues in existence by force of this subsection as a\nbody corporate, under and subject to the provisions of this Act,\nunder the name Australian Broadcasting Corporation.\nNote:\nThe Public Governance, Performance and Accountability Act 2013\napplies to the Corporation. That Act deals with matters relating to\ncorporate Commonwealth entities, including reporting and the use and\nmanagement of public resources.\n(2) The Corporation:\n(a) shall have a seal; and\n(b) may sue and be sued.\n(3) All courts, judges and persons acting judicially shall take judicial\nnotice of the imprint of the seal of the Corporation appearing on a\ndocument and shall presume that the document was duly sealed.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The body corporate that was, immediately before the commencing\nday, in existence by virtue of section 30 of the Broadcasting and\nTelevision Act 1942 under the name Australian Broadcasting\nCommission continues in existence by force of this subsection as a\nbody corporate, under and subject to the provisions of this Act,\nunder the name Australian Broadcasting Corporation.\nNote:\nThe Public Governance, Performance and Accountability Act 2013\napplies to the Corporation. That Act deals with matters relating to\ncorporate Commonwealth entities, including reporting and the use and\nmanagement of public resources.\n(2) The Corporation:\n(a) shall have a seal; and\n(b) may sue and be sued.\n(3) All courts, judges and persons acting judicially shall take judicial\nnotice of the imprint of the seal of the Corporation appearing on a\ndocument and shall presume that the document was duly sealed.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-5-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-5-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-5-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "bf52e39e36be15d83351712e08f2617b4cccfb26572339309a32e3b539f4c53a"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983#sec-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "5 Australian Broadcasting Corporation",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 12,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The body corporate that was, immediately before the commencing\nday, in existence by virtue of section 30 of the Broadcasting and\nTelevision Act 1942 under the name Australian Broadcasting\nCommission continues in existence by force of this subsection as a\nbody corporate, under and subject to the provisions of this Act,\nunder the name Australian Broadcasting Corporation.\nNote:\nThe Public Governance, Performance and Accountability Act 2013\napplies to the Corporation. That Act deals with matters relating to\ncorporate Commonwealth entities, including reporting and the use and\nmanagement of public resources.\n(2) The Corporation:\n(a) shall have a seal; and\n(b) may sue and be sued.\n(3) All courts, judges and persons acting judicially shall take judicial\nnotice of the imprint of the seal of the Corporation appearing on a\ndocument and shall presume that the document was duly sealed."
    },
