        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(ii) broadcasting programs of an educational nature;\n\n\nEstablishment, functions and management of the Corporation  Part II\n\nSection 6\nAustralian Broadcasting Corporation Act 1983"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-6-ss-1-logic-diffusion-4",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Diffusion"
      },
      "cml:operator": "SPREADS",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Spreads information about Australia",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::diffusion",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(i) encourage awareness of Australia and an international understanding of Australian attitudes on world affairs;"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-6-ss-1-logic-cogai-5",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:CogAI"
      },
      "cml:operator": "REQUIRES",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Requires digital media services",
      "cml:executionSurface": "sparql_library::parsers::chk_parser",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(b) to provide digital media services;"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-6-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "6(2) Charter of the Corporation",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983#sec-6-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983.pdf, p.12",
      "values:originalText": "(2) In the provision by the Corporation of its broadcasting services\nwithin Australia:\n(a) the Corporation shall take account of:\n(i) the broadcasting services provided by the commercial\nand community sectors of the Australian broadcasting\nsystem;\n(ii) the standards from time to time determined by the\nACMA in respect of broadcasting services;\n(iii) the responsibility of the Corporation as the provider of\nan independent national broadcasting service to provide\na balance between broadcasting programs of wide\nappeal and specialized broadcasting programs;\n(iv) the multicultural character of the Australian community;\nand\n(v) in connection with the provision of broadcasting\nprograms of an educational nature—the responsibilities\nof the States in relation to education; and\n(b) the Corporation shall take all such measures, being measures\nconsistent with the obligations of the Corporation under\nparagraph (a), as, in the opinion of the Board, will be",
      "skos:definition": "(2) In the provision by the Corporation of its broadcasting services\nwithin Australia:\n(a) the Corporation shall take account of:\n(i) the broadcasting services provided by the commercial\nand community sectors of the Australian broadcasting\nsystem;\n(ii) the standards from time to time determined by the\nACMA in respect of broadcasting services;\n(iii) the responsibility of the Corporation as the provider of\nan independent national broadcasting service to provide\na balance between broadcasting programs of wide\nappeal and specialized broadcasting programs;\n(iv) the multicultural character of the Australian community;\nand\n(v) in connection with the provision of broadcasting\nprograms of an educational nature—the responsibilities\nof the States in relation to education; and\n(b) the Corporation shall take all such measures, being measures\nconsistent with the obligations of the Corporation under\nparagraph (a), as, in the opinion of the Board, will be",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-6"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-6-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-6-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "90ca485039c5418efc789eae96e2c31704ea5f7c1688876eac69d1e065a350f0",
      "skos:note": "The Corporation must take account of certain factors when providing broadcasting services.",
      "dc:description": "Yes"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983#sec-6-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "6(2) Charter of the Corporation",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 12,
      "values:originalText": "(2) In the provision by the Corporation of its broadcasting services\nwithin Australia:\n(a) the Corporation shall take account of:\n(i) the broadcasting services provided by the commercial\nand community sectors of the Australian broadcasting\nsystem;\n(ii) the standards from time to time determined by the\nACMA in respect of broadcasting services;\n(iii) the responsibility of the Corporation as the provider of\nan independent national broadcasting service to provide\na balance between broadcasting programs of wide\nappeal and specialized broadcasting programs;\n(iv) the multicultural character of the Australian community;\nand\n(v) in connection with the provision of broadcasting\nprograms of an educational nature—the responsibilities\nof the States in relation to education; and\n(b) the Corporation shall take all such measures, being measures\nconsistent with the obligations of the Corporation under\nparagraph (a), as, in the opinion of the Board, will be"
    },
