    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-11",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "11 Advisory Councils and committees",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983#sec-11"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983.pdf, p.16",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Board shall establish an Advisory Council under the name\nAustralian Broadcasting Corporation Advisory Council.\n(2) The Board may also establish:\n(a) an Advisory Council in relation to any State;\n(b) an Advisory Council in relation to any Territory; and\n(c) an Advisory Council in relation to any region of Australia.\n(3) The function of the Australian Broadcasting Corporation Advisory\nCouncil is, either on its own initiative or at the request of the\nBoard, to advise the Board on matters relating to the Corporation’s\nbroadcasting programs.\n(4) The function of an Advisory Council established under\nsubsection (2) in relation to a State, Territory or region is, either on\nits own initiative or at the request of the Australian Broadcasting\nCorporation Advisory Council, to advise the Australian\nBroadcasting Corporation Advisory Council on matters relating to\nthe Corporation’s broadcasting programs in that State, Territory or\nregion.\n(5) An Advisory Council shall consist of such persons as the Board\nfrom time to time appoints.\n\n\nEstablishment, functions and management of the Corporation  Part II\n\nSection 11\nAustralian Broadcasting Corporation Act 1983\nCompilation date: 18/02/2022\nRegistered: 23/02/2022\n(6) In making appointments to the Australian Broadcasting\nCorporation Advisory Council, the Board shall have regard to the\ndesirability of including in the membership of that Advisory\nCouncil a broad representation of the Australian community.\n(7) In the case of each Advisory Council, the Board shall appoint one\nof the members of the Advisory Council to be the Chairperson of\nthe Advisory Council and another of the members of the Advisory\nCouncil to be the Deputy Chairperson of the Advisory Council.\n(8) In addition to Advisory Councils, the Board may establish advisory\ncommittees, consisting of such persons as the Board appoints, to\nfurnish advice to the Board on particular matters or classes of\nmatters relating to the functions of the Corporation.\n(9) The Board may determine:\n(a) the manner in which an Advisory Council or advisory\ncommittee is to perform its functions; and\n(b) the procedure to be followed at or in relation to meetings of\nan Advisory Council or advisory committee, including\nmatters with respect to:\n(i) the convening of meetings of the Advisory Council or\nadvisory committee;\n(ii) the number of members of the Advisory Council or\nadvisory committee who are to constitute a quorum;\n(iii) the selection of a member of the Advisory Council or\nadvisory committee to preside at meetings of the\nAdvisory Council or advisory committee at which the\nChairperson and the Deputy Chairperson of the\nAdvisory Council or advisory committee are not\npresent; and\n(iv) the manner in which questions arising at a meeting of\nthe Advisory Council or advisory committee are to be\ndecided;\nand the Managing Director shall notify each Advisory Council or\nadvisory committee in writing of any determination by the Board\nunder this subsection in relation to that Advisory Council or\nadvisory committee.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Board shall establish an Advisory Council under the name\nAustralian Broadcasting Corporation Advisory Council.\n(2) The Board may also establish:\n(a) an Advisory Council in relation to any State;\n(b) an Advisory Council in relation to any Territory; and\n(c) an Advisory Council in relation to any region of Australia.\n(3) The function of the Australian Broadcasting Corporation Advisory\nCouncil is, either on its own initiative or at the request of the\nBoard, to advise the Board on matters relating to the Corporation’s\nbroadcasting programs.\n(4) The function of an Advisory Council established under\nsubsection (2) in relation to a State, Territory or region is, either on\nits own initiative or at the request of the Australian Broadcasting\nCorporation Advisory Council, to advise the Australian\nBroadcasting Corporation Advisory Council on matters relating to\nthe Corporation’s broadcasting programs in that State, Territory or\nregion.\n(5) An Advisory Council shall consist of such persons as the Board\nfrom time to time appoints.\n\n\nEstablishment, functions and management of the Corporation  Part II\n\nSection 11\nAustralian Broadcasting Corporation Act 1983\nCompilation date: 18/02/2022\nRegistered: 23/02/2022\n(6) In making appointments to the Australian Broadcasting\nCorporation Advisory Council, the Board shall have regard to the\ndesirability of including in the membership of that Advisory\nCouncil a broad representation of the Australian community.\n(7) In the case of each Advisory Council, the Board shall appoint one\nof the members of the Advisory Council to be the Chairperson of\nthe Advisory Council and another of the members of the Advisory\nCouncil to be the Deputy Chairperson of the Advisory Council.\n(8) In addition to Advisory Councils, the Board may establish advisory\ncommittees, consisting of such persons as the Board appoints, to\nfurnish advice to the Board on particular matters or classes of\nmatters relating to the functions of the Corporation.\n(9) The Board may dete",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-11-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-11-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-11-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-11-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-11-ss-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-11-ss-6"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-11-ss-7"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-11-ss-8"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-11-ss-9"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "461f4b6888aedaa007c3138606a5fdd9f54dc893f09600b07be99849e5b10f67"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983#sec-11",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "11 Advisory Councils and committees",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 16,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Board shall establish an Advisory Council under the name\nAustralian Broadcasting Corporation Advisory Council.\n(2) The Board may also establish:\n(a) an Advisory Council in relation to any State;\n(b) an Advisory Council in relation to any Territory; and\n(c) an Advisory Council in relation to any region of Australia.\n(3) The function of the Australian Broadcasting Corporation Advisory\nCouncil is, either on its own initiative or at the request of the\nBoard, to advise the Board on matters relating to the Corporation’s\nbroadcasting programs.\n(4) The function of an Advisory Council established under\nsubsection (2) in relation to a State, Territory or region is, either on\nits own initiative or at the request of the Australian Broadcasting\nCorporation Advisory Council, to advise the Australian\nBroadcasting Corporation Advisory Council on matters relating to\nthe Corporation’s broadcasting programs in that State, Territory or\nregion.\n(5) An Advisory Council shall consist of such persons as the Board\nfrom time to time appoints.\n\n\nEstablishment, functions and management of the Corporation  Part II\n\nSection 11\nAustralian Broadcasting Corporation Act 1983\nCompilation date: 18/02/2022\nRegistered: 23/02/2022\n(6) In making appointments to the Australian Broadcasting\nCorporation Advisory Council, the Board shall have regard to the\ndesirability of including in the membership of that Advisory\nCouncil a broad representation of the Australian community.\n(7) In the case of each Advisory Council, the Board shall appoint one\nof the members of the Advisory Council to be the Chairperson of\nthe Advisory Council and another of the members of the Advisory\nCouncil to be the Deputy Chairperson of the Advisory Council.\n(8) In addition to Advisory Councils, the Board may establish advisory\ncommittees, consisting of such persons as the Board appoints, to\nfurnish advice to the Board on particular matters or classes of\nmatters relating to the functions of the Corporation.\n(9) The Board may determine:\n(a) the manner in which an Advisory Council or advisory\ncommittee is to perform its functions; and\n(b) the procedure to be followed at or in relation to meetings of\nan Advisory Council or advisory committee, including\nmatters with respect to:\n(i) the convening of meetings of the Advisory Council or\nadvisory committee;\n(ii) the number of members of the Advisory Council or\nadvisory committee who are to constitute a quorum;\n(iii) the selection of a member of the Advisory Council or\nadvisory committee to preside at meetings of the\nAdvisory Council or advisory committee at which the\nChairperson and the Deputy Chairperson of the\nAdvisory Council or advisory committee are not\npresent; and\n(iv) the manner in which questions arising at a meeting of\nthe Advisory Council or advisory committee are to be\ndecided;\nand the Managing Director shall notify each Advisory Council or\nadvisory committee in writing of any determination by the Board\nunder this subsection in relation to that Advisory Council or\nadvisory committee."
    },
