    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-12",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "12 Membership of Board",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983#sec-12"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983.pdf, p.19",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Board shall consist of:\n(a) the Managing Director; and\n(b) the Chairperson; and\n(ba) the staff-elected Director; and\n(c) not fewer than 4 nor more than 6 other Directors.\n(2) A Director referred to in paragraph (1)(b) or (c) shall be appointed\nby the Governor-General and, subject to sections 16 and 18, holds\noffice on a part-time basis for such period, not exceeding 5 years,\nas is specified in the instrument of his or her appointment, but is\neligible for re-appointment.\n(2A) The sum of the periods for which a person holds either or both of\nthe following offices must not exceed 10 years:\n(a) an office referred to in paragraph (1)(b);\n(b) an office referred to in paragraph (1)(c).\nExample 1:Assume a person holds office as Chairperson for an initial period of 5\nyears and then holds office as Chairperson for a further period of 5\nyears.\nThe person cannot hold office as Chairperson again and cannot hold\noffice as a Director referred to in paragraph (1)(c).\nExample 2:Assume a person holds office as a Director referred to in\nparagraph (1)(c) for a period of 5 years and then holds office as\nChairperson for a period of 3 years.\nThe person may now hold office as Chairperson, or as a Director\nreferred to in paragraph (1)(c), for a maximum period of 2 years.\n(3) The Governor-General shall appoint one of the non-executive\nDirectors to be the Deputy Chairperson of the Board.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Board shall consist of:\n(a) the Managing Director; and\n(b) the Chairperson; and\n(ba) the staff-elected Director; and\n(c) not fewer than 4 nor more than 6 other Directors.\n(2) A Director referred to in paragraph (1)(b) or (c) shall be appointed\nby the Governor-General and, subject to sections 16 and 18, holds\noffice on a part-time basis for such period, not exceeding 5 years,\nas is specified in the instrument of his or her appointment, but is\neligible for re-appointment.\n(2A) The sum of the periods for which a person holds either or both of\nthe following offices must not exceed 10 years:\n(a) an office referred to in paragraph (1)(b);\n(b) an office referred to in paragraph (1)(c).\nExample 1:Assume a person holds office as Chairperson for an initial period of 5\nyears and then holds office as Chairperson for a further period of 5\nyears.\nThe person cannot hold office as Chairperson again and cannot hold\noffice as a Director referred to in paragraph (1)(c).\nExample 2:Assume a person holds office as a Director referred to in\nparagraph (1)(c) for a period of 5 years and then holds office as\nChairperson for a period of 3 years.\nThe person may now hold office as Chairperson, or as a Director\nreferred to in paragraph (1)(c), for a maximum period of 2 years.\n(3) The Governor-General shall appoint one of the non-executive\nDirectors to be the Deputy Chairperson of the Board.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-12-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-12-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-12-ss-2a"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-12-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "566000986738a680e70472948f89b69e0a4e198dd9ceda6477d649e6de5f439b"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983#sec-12",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "12 Membership of Board",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 19,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Board shall consist of:\n(a) the Managing Director; and\n(b) the Chairperson; and\n(ba) the staff-elected Director; and\n(c) not fewer than 4 nor more than 6 other Directors.\n(2) A Director referred to in paragraph (1)(b) or (c) shall be appointed\nby the Governor-General and, subject to sections 16 and 18, holds\noffice on a part-time basis for such period, not exceeding 5 years,\nas is specified in the instrument of his or her appointment, but is\neligible for re-appointment.\n(2A) The sum of the periods for which a person holds either or both of\nthe following offices must not exceed 10 years:\n(a) an office referred to in paragraph (1)(b);\n(b) an office referred to in paragraph (1)(c).\nExample 1:Assume a person holds office as Chairperson for an initial period of 5\nyears and then holds office as Chairperson for a further period of 5\nyears.\nThe person cannot hold office as Chairperson again and cannot hold\noffice as a Director referred to in paragraph (1)(c).\nExample 2:Assume a person holds office as a Director referred to in\nparagraph (1)(c) for a period of 5 years and then holds office as\nChairperson for a period of 3 years.\nThe person may now hold office as Chairperson, or as a Director\nreferred to in paragraph (1)(c), for a maximum period of 2 years.\n(3) The Governor-General shall appoint one of the non-executive\nDirectors to be the Deputy Chairperson of the Board."
    },
