      "dc:source": "australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983.pdf, p.25",
      "values:originalText": "(2) If:\n(a) a non-executive Director becomes bankrupt, takes steps to\ntake the benefit of any law for the relief of bankrupt or\ninsolvent debtors, compounds with one or more of his or her\ncreditors or makes an assignment of his or her remuneration\nfor the benefit of one or more of his or her creditors; or\n(aa) the staff-elected Director ceases to be eligible to hold office\nas the staff-elected Director; or\n(b) the Chairperson, or a Director acting as Chairperson, is\nabsent, except with the leave of the Minister, from 3\nconsecutive meetings of the Board; or",
      "skos:definition": "(2) If:\n(a) a non-executive Director becomes bankrupt, takes steps to\ntake the benefit of any law for the relief of bankrupt or\ninsolvent debtors, compounds with one or more of his or her\ncreditors or makes an assignment of his or her remuneration\nfor the benefit of one or more of his or her creditors; or\n(aa) the staff-elected Director ceases to be eligible to hold office\nas the staff-elected Director; or\n(b) the Chairperson, or a Director acting as Chairperson, is\nabsent, except with the leave of the Minister, from 3\nconsecutive meetings of the Board; or",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-18-2"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-18-2-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-18-2-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "152a1a8d546beed514ffe3054fb000a76bbec4f3d0c063872754fc4e2b687e83",
      "skos:note": "Prohibition on certain actions by non-executive Directors and staff-elected Directors"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983#sec-18-2-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "18(2) Removal from office of non-executive Directors",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 25,
      "values:originalText": "(2) If:\n(a) a non-executive Director becomes bankrupt, takes steps to\ntake the benefit of any law for the relief of bankrupt or\ninsolvent debtors, compounds with one or more of his or her\ncreditors or makes an assignment of his or her remuneration\nfor the benefit of one or more of his or her creditors; or\n(aa) the staff-elected Director ceases to be eligible to hold office\nas the staff-elected Director; or\n(b) the Chairperson, or a Director acting as Chairperson, is\nabsent, except with the leave of the Minister, from 3\nconsecutive meetings of the Board; or"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-18-2-ss-2-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
