    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-21",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "21 Acting non-executive Directors",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983#sec-21"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983.pdf, p.28",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If a non-executive Director is, or is expected to be, absent from\nduty or from Australia or, for any other reason, unable to perform\nthe functions of his or her office, the Governor-General may\nappoint a person to act as a non-executive Director during the\nperiod of the absence or inability.\nNote:\nFor rules that apply to acting appointments, see sections 33AB and\n33A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.\n(2) The Governor-General may:\n(a) determine the terms and conditions of appointment,\nexcluding remuneration and allowances, of a person acting as\na non-executive Director; and\n(b) terminate such an appointment at any time.\n(3) A person acting as a non-executive Director shall be paid the same\nremuneration and allowances as are payable to a non-executive\nDirector.\n(7) In this section, non-executive Director does not include the\nstaff-elected Director.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If a non-executive Director is, or is expected to be, absent from\nduty or from Australia or, for any other reason, unable to perform\nthe functions of his or her office, the Governor-General may\nappoint a person to act as a non-executive Director during the\nperiod of the absence or inability.\nNote:\nFor rules that apply to acting appointments, see sections 33AB and\n33A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.\n(2) The Governor-General may:\n(a) determine the terms and conditions of appointment,\nexcluding remuneration and allowances, of a person acting as\na non-executive Director; and\n(b) terminate such an appointment at any time.\n(3) A person acting as a non-executive Director shall be paid the same\nremuneration and allowances as are payable to a non-executive\nDirector.\n(7) In this section, non-executive Director does not include the\nstaff-elected Director.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-21-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-21-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-21-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-21-ss-7"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "fdce56b929c95c89a62c747c277a094d9bee603ec28ce1e7a971b2a6806c367a"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983#sec-21",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "21 Acting non-executive Directors",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 28,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If a non-executive Director is, or is expected to be, absent from\nduty or from Australia or, for any other reason, unable to perform\nthe functions of his or her office, the Governor-General may\nappoint a person to act as a non-executive Director during the\nperiod of the absence or inability.\nNote:\nFor rules that apply to acting appointments, see sections 33AB and\n33A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.\n(2) The Governor-General may:\n(a) determine the terms and conditions of appointment,\nexcluding remuneration and allowances, of a person acting as\na non-executive Director; and\n(b) terminate such an appointment at any time.\n(3) A person acting as a non-executive Director shall be paid the same\nremuneration and allowances as are payable to a non-executive\nDirector.\n(7) In this section, non-executive Director does not include the\nstaff-elected Director."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-21-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "21(1) Acting non-executive Directors",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983#sec-21-ss-1"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983.pdf, p.28",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If a non-executive Director is, or is expected to be, absent from\nduty or from Australia or, for any other reason, unable to perform\nthe functions of his or her office, the Governor-General may\nappoint a person to act as a non-executive Director during the\nperiod of the absence or inability.\nNote:\nFor rules that apply to acting appointments, see sections 33AB and\n33A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If a non-executive Director is, or is expected to be, absent from\nduty or from Australia or, for any other reason, unable to perform\nthe functions of his or her office, the Governor-General may\nappoint a person to act as a non-executive Director during the\nperiod of the absence or inability.\nNote:\nFor rules that apply to acting appointments, see sections 33AB and\n33A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-21"
      },
