          "@id": "concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-21-ss-1-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "6737faa759003f30fb355bc5963bc4e5a0fb468a6c5c9dc6c36ba0d3a925338a",
      "skos:note": "Governor-General may appoint acting non-executive Director in absence or inability."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983#sec-21-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "21(1) Acting non-executive Directors",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 28,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If a non-executive Director is, or is expected to be, absent from\nduty or from Australia or, for any other reason, unable to perform\nthe functions of his or her office, the Governor-General may\nappoint a person to act as a non-executive Director during the\nperiod of the absence or inability.\nNote:\nFor rules that apply to acting appointments, see sections 33AB and\n33A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901."
    },
