    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-23-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "23 Delegation by Corporation",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983#sec-23-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983.pdf, p.30",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Corporation may, either generally or as otherwise provided by\nthe instrument of delegation, by writing under its seal, delegate to a\nDirector or to an employee of the Corporation all or any of its\npowers under this Act, the regulations or the rules, other than this\npower of delegation.\n(2) A power so delegated, when exercised by the delegate, shall, for\nthe purposes of this Act, the regulations or the rules, be deemed to\nhave been exercised by the Corporation.\n(3) A delegation of a power under this section does not prevent the\nexercise of the power by the Corporation.\n(4) A reference in this section to a Director shall, if a person is acting\nas a Director, be construed as including a reference to a person so\nacting.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Corporation may, either generally or as otherwise provided by\nthe instrument of delegation, by writing under its seal, delegate to a\nDirector or to an employee of the Corporation all or any of its\npowers under this Act, the regulations or the rules, other than this\npower of delegation.\n(2) A power so delegated, when exercised by the delegate, shall, for\nthe purposes of this Act, the regulations or the rules, be deemed to\nhave been exercised by the Corporation.\n(3) A delegation of a power under this section does not prevent the\nexercise of the power by the Corporation.\n(4) A reference in this section to a Director shall, if a person is acting\nas a Director, be construed as including a reference to a person so\nacting.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-23-2-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-23-2-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-23-2-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-23-2-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9cbc71ff6d1b03b272000705130aa4452b1e9a4be331f3da03f1dd8f5722da30"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983#sec-23-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "23 Delegation by Corporation",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 30,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Corporation may, either generally or as otherwise provided by\nthe instrument of delegation, by writing under its seal, delegate to a\nDirector or to an employee of the Corporation all or any of its\npowers under this Act, the regulations or the rules, other than this\npower of delegation.\n(2) A power so delegated, when exercised by the delegate, shall, for\nthe purposes of this Act, the regulations or the rules, be deemed to\nhave been exercised by the Corporation.\n(3) A delegation of a power under this section does not prevent the\nexercise of the power by the Corporation.\n(4) A reference in this section to a Director shall, if a person is acting\nas a Director, be construed as including a reference to a person so\nacting."
    },
