          "@id": "concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-24n-ss-2-logic-argumentation-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-24n-ss-2-logic-diffusion-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "445864ec414b3c9b706237eaae4c1ee0785c86e8f8bfbe5ff27f3ad6eadd11a5",
      "skos:note": "Termination of appointment under certain conditions."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983#sec-24n-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "24N(2) Termination of appointment",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 38,
      "values:originalText": "(2) The Secretary of the Prime Minister’s Department may terminate\nthe appointment of a member of the Nomination Panel if:\n\n\nMerit-based appointment of non-executive Directors  Part IIIA\nConstitution and membership of Nomination Panel  Division 2\nSection 24P\nAustralian Broadcasting Corporation Act 1983\nCompilation date: 18/02/2022\nRegistered: 23/02/2022\n(a) the member:\n(i) becomes bankrupt; or\n(ii) applies to take the benefit of any law for the relief of\nbankrupt or insolvent debtors; or\n(iii) compounds with his or her creditors; or\n(iv) makes an assignment of his or her remuneration for the\nbenefit of his or her creditors; or\n(b) the member is absent, except on leave of absence, from 3\nconsecutive meetings of the Nomination Panel; or\n(c) the member fails, without reasonable excuse, to comply with\nsection 24K or 24L (disclosure of interests)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-24n-ss-2-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
      "cml:modality": {
