    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-28",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "28 Orchestras, bands, concerts etc.",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983#sec-28"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983.pdf, p.49",
      "values:originalText": "For the purposes of the performance of its functions, the\nCorporation may:",
      "skos:definition": "For the purposes of the performance of its functions, the\nCorporation may:",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-28-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9d01ce2a1fcfbfa4bf8e41c137f7b4aa052f063f59e8823b87cfcbbc70ad2db9",
      "skos:note": "Corporation may perform certain functions"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983#sec-28",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "28 Orchestras, bands, concerts etc.",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 49,
      "values:originalText": "For the purposes of the performance of its functions, the\nCorporation may:"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-28-norm",
      "@type": "values:Undertaking",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-28"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-29",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "29 Publication of journals etc. and making etc. of sound recordings",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983#sec-29"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983.pdf, p.50",
      "values:originalText": "etc.\n(1) The Corporation may:\n(a) compile, prepare, issue, circulate and distribute literary\nmaterial (including the program schedules of broadcasting\nservices provided by the Corporation and other persons); and\n(b) make, promote, circulate and distribute:\n(i) cinematograph films and sound recordings of, or\nrelating to:\n(A) programs of the Corporation (whether or not\nbroadcast); and\n(B) public concerts and other public entertainment\nreferred to in paragraph 28(b); and\n(ii) any article or thing bearing a mark that is associated\nwith any program, concert or entertainment referred to\nin subparagraph (i).\n(2) The Corporation may from time to time determine charges payable\nin respect of any matter or activity referred to in subsection (1),\nwith a view to raising as much net revenue as is practicable, having\nregard to the proper performance of its functions and to the matter\nor activity concerned.\n(3) A program schedule referred to in paragraph (1)(a) shall be made\navailable at an office of the Corporation on equal terms to the\npublishers of any newspaper, magazine or journal published in\nAustralia before the publication of the program schedule pursuant\nto subsection (1).\n\n\nPowers and duties of the Corporation  Part IV\n\nSection 29A\nAustralian Broadcasting Corporation Act 1983\nCompilation date: 18/02/2022\nRegistered: 23/02/2022\n(4) In this section, mark includes a symbol, design, colour, device,\nbrand, heading, label, sign, ticket, name, signature, word, letter,\nnumeral, drawing or picture, or any combination of the foregoing.",
      "skos:definition": "etc.\n(1) The Corporation may:\n(a) compile, prepare, issue, circulate and distribute literary\nmaterial (including the program schedules of broadcasting\nservices provided by the Corporation and other persons); and\n(b) make, promote, circulate and distribute:\n(i) cinematograph films and sound recordings of, or\nrelating to:\n(A) programs of the Corporation (whether or not\nbroadcast); and\n(B) public concerts and other public entertainment\nreferred to in paragraph 28(b); and\n(ii) any article or thing bearing a mark that is associated\nwith any program, concert or entertainment referred to\nin subparagraph (i).\n(2) The Corporation may from time to time determine charges payable\nin respect of any matter or activity referred to in subsection (1),\nwith a view to raising as much net revenue as is practicable, having\nregard to the proper performance of its functions and to the matter\nor activity concerned.\n(3) A program schedule referred to in paragraph (1)(a) shall be made\navailable at an office of the Corporation on equal terms to the\npublishers of any newspaper, magazine or journal published in\nAustralia before the publication of the program schedule pursuant\nto subsection (1).\n\n\nPowers and duties of the Corporation  Part IV\n\nSection 29A\nAustralian Broadcasting Corporation Act 1983\nCompilation date: 18/02/2022\nRegistered: 23/02/2022\n(4) In this section, mark includes a symbol, design, colour, device,\nbrand, heading, label, sign, ticket, name, signature, word, letter,\nnumeral, drawing or picture, or any combination of the foregoing.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-29-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-29-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-29-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-29-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "41b387a9617d9ffde9dc713bb94531bfc48d834db2fdc78d61c2040332d7bd35"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983#sec-29",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "29 Publication of journals etc. and making etc. of sound recordings",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 50,
      "values:originalText": "etc.\n(1) The Corporation may:\n(a) compile, prepare, issue, circulate and distribute literary\nmaterial (including the program schedules of broadcasting\nservices provided by the Corporation and other persons); and\n(b) make, promote, circulate and distribute:\n(i) cinematograph films and sound recordings of, or\nrelating to:\n(A) programs of the Corporation (whether or not\nbroadcast); and\n(B) public concerts and other public entertainment\nreferred to in paragraph 28(b); and\n(ii) any article or thing bearing a mark that is associated\nwith any program, concert or entertainment referred to\nin subparagraph (i).\n(2) The Corporation may from time to time determine charges payable\nin respect of any matter or activity referred to in subsection (1),\nwith a view to raising as much net revenue as is practicable, having\nregard to the proper performance of its functions and to the matter\nor activity concerned.\n(3) A program schedule referred to in paragraph (1)(a) shall be made\navailable at an office of the Corporation on equal terms to the\npublishers of any newspaper, magazine or journal published in\nAustralia before the publication of the program schedule pursuant\nto subsection (1).\n\n\nPowers and duties of the Corporation  Part IV\n\nSection 29A\nAustralian Broadcasting Corporation Act 1983\nCompilation date: 18/02/2022\nRegistered: 23/02/2022\n(4) In this section, mark includes a symbol, design, colour, device,\nbrand, heading, label, sign, ticket, name, signature, word, letter,\nnumeral, drawing or picture, or any combination of the foregoing."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-29-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "29(1) Publication of journals etc. and making etc. of sound recordings",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
