    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-31",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "31 Advertisements",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983#sec-31"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983.pdf, p.51",
      "values:originalText": "Broadcasting services\n(1) The Corporation shall not broadcast advertisements on any of the\nCorporation’s broadcasting services.\n(2) Subsection (1) does not prevent the Corporation, if the Board\nthinks fit, from broadcasting:\n(a) any announcement relating to any activity or proposed\nactivity of the Corporation;\n(b) a program supplied by any organization or person engaged in\nartistic, literary, musical or theatrical production or in\neducational pursuits; or\n(c) a program supplied by any organization or person other than\na program that is, in the opinion of the Corporation, being\nused as an advertisement;\nor from broadcasting any matter the broadcasting of which is\ndirected by the Minister pursuant to subsection 78(1).\n(3) Subsection (1) does not apply to:\n(a) the broadcasting of any matter by the Corporation’s\ninternational television service and its associated audio\nchannels outside Australia; or\n(b) the broadcasting of any matter by the Corporation’s\ninternational television service and its associated audio\nchannels inside Australia that is merely incidental to the\nbroadcasting of the matter outside Australia.",
      "skos:definition": "Broadcasting services\n(1) The Corporation shall not broadcast advertisements on any of the\nCorporation’s broadcasting services.\n(2) Subsection (1) does not prevent the Corporation, if the Board\nthinks fit, from broadcasting:\n(a) any announcement relating to any activity or proposed\nactivity of the Corporation;\n(b) a program supplied by any organization or person engaged in\nartistic, literary, musical or theatrical production or in\neducational pursuits; or\n(c) a program supplied by any organization or person other than\na program that is, in the opinion of the Corporation, being\nused as an advertisement;\nor from broadcasting any matter the broadcasting of which is\ndirected by the Minister pursuant to subsection 78(1).\n(3) Subsection (1) does not apply to:\n(a) the broadcasting of any matter by the Corporation’s\ninternational television service and its associated audio\nchannels outside Australia; or\n(b) the broadcasting of any matter by the Corporation’s\ninternational television service and its associated audio\nchannels inside Australia that is merely incidental to the\nbroadcasting of the matter outside Australia.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-31-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-31-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-31-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "4dfe3e7f5b50ffa144d045a9be98acf6acb7ccaf8cfa3007a820f2f7905431d4"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983#sec-31",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "31 Advertisements",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 51,
      "values:originalText": "Broadcasting services\n(1) The Corporation shall not broadcast advertisements on any of the\nCorporation’s broadcasting services.\n(2) Subsection (1) does not prevent the Corporation, if the Board\nthinks fit, from broadcasting:\n(a) any announcement relating to any activity or proposed\nactivity of the Corporation;\n(b) a program supplied by any organization or person engaged in\nartistic, literary, musical or theatrical production or in\neducational pursuits; or\n(c) a program supplied by any organization or person other than\na program that is, in the opinion of the Corporation, being\nused as an advertisement;\nor from broadcasting any matter the broadcasting of which is\ndirected by the Minister pursuant to subsection 78(1).\n(3) Subsection (1) does not apply to:\n(a) the broadcasting of any matter by the Corporation’s\ninternational television service and its associated audio\nchannels outside Australia; or\n(b) the broadcasting of any matter by the Corporation’s\ninternational television service and its associated audio\nchannels inside Australia that is merely incidental to the\nbroadcasting of the matter outside Australia."
    },
