    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-31b",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "31B Matters to be included in corporate plans",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983#sec-31b"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983.pdf, p.54",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Each corporate plan prepared by the Board under section 35 of the\nPublic Governance, Performance and Accountability Act 2013\nmust:\n(a) outline the overall strategies and policies that the Corporation\nand its subsidiaries are to follow to ensure that the Board\nfulfils its duties under section 8; and\n(b) include a forecast of the revenue and expenditure of the\nCorporation and its subsidiaries, including a forecast of\ncapital expenditure and borrowings; and\n(c) include such other matters as are prescribed in the regulations\nmade for the purposes of this Act.\n(2) Subsection 35(3) of the Public Governance, Performance and\nAccountability Act 2013 (which deals with the Australian\nGovernment’s key priorities and objectives) does not apply to a\ncorporate plan prepared by the Board.\n(3) In this section:\nsubsidiary means a prescribed company within the meaning of\nsection 25A of this Act that the Corporation controls.\n(4) For the purposes of the application of section 35 of the Public\nGovernance, Performance and Accountability Act 2013 in relation\nto the Corporation, subsidiary is taken to have the meaning given\nby subsection (3) of this section, despite the definition of\nsubsidiary in section 8 of that Act.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Each corporate plan prepared by the Board under section 35 of the\nPublic Governance, Performance and Accountability Act 2013\nmust:\n(a) outline the overall strategies and policies that the Corporation\nand its subsidiaries are to follow to ensure that the Board\nfulfils its duties under section 8; and\n(b) include a forecast of the revenue and expenditure of the\nCorporation and its subsidiaries, including a forecast of\ncapital expenditure and borrowings; and\n(c) include such other matters as are prescribed in the regulations\nmade for the purposes of this Act.\n(2) Subsection 35(3) of the Public Governance, Performance and\nAccountability Act 2013 (which deals with the Australian\nGovernment’s key priorities and objectives) does not apply to a\ncorporate plan prepared by the Board.\n(3) In this section:\nsubsidiary means a prescribed company within the meaning of\nsection 25A of this Act that the Corporation controls.\n(4) For the purposes of the application of section 35 of the Public\nGovernance, Performance and Accountability Act 2013 in relation\nto the Corporation, subsidiary is taken to have the meaning given\nby subsection (3) of this section, despite the definition of\nsubsidiary in section 8 of that Act.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-31b-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-31b-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-31b-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-31b-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "1f7c890e24b8a12197a7b6fce1a75669f0f916aa0739327ebb89209b3dd45366"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983#sec-31b",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "31B Matters to be included in corporate plans",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 54,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Each corporate plan prepared by the Board under section 35 of the\nPublic Governance, Performance and Accountability Act 2013\nmust:\n(a) outline the overall strategies and policies that the Corporation\nand its subsidiaries are to follow to ensure that the Board\nfulfils its duties under section 8; and\n(b) include a forecast of the revenue and expenditure of the\nCorporation and its subsidiaries, including a forecast of\ncapital expenditure and borrowings; and\n(c) include such other matters as are prescribed in the regulations\nmade for the purposes of this Act.\n(2) Subsection 35(3) of the Public Governance, Performance and\nAccountability Act 2013 (which deals with the Australian\nGovernment’s key priorities and objectives) does not apply to a\ncorporate plan prepared by the Board.\n(3) In this section:\nsubsidiary means a prescribed company within the meaning of\nsection 25A of this Act that the Corporation controls.\n(4) For the purposes of the application of section 35 of the Public\nGovernance, Performance and Accountability Act 2013 in relation\nto the Corporation, subsidiary is taken to have the meaning given\nby subsection (3) of this section, despite the definition of\nsubsidiary in section 8 of that Act."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-31b-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "31B(1) Matters to be included in corporate plans",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983#sec-31b-ss-1"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983.pdf, p.54",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Each corporate plan prepared by the Board under section 35 of the\nPublic Governance, Performance and Accountability Act 2013\nmust:\n(a) outline the overall strategies and policies that the Corporation\nand its subsidiaries are to follow to ensure that the Board\nfulfils its duties under section 8; and\n(b) include a forecast of the revenue and expenditure of the\nCorporation and its subsidiaries, including a forecast of\ncapital expenditure and borrowings; and\n(c) include such other matters as are prescribed in the regulations\nmade for the purposes of this Act.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Each corporate plan prepared by the Board under section 35 of the\nPublic Governance, Performance and Accountability Act 2013\nmust:\n(a) outline the overall strategies and policies that the Corporation\nand its subsidiaries are to follow to ensure that the Board\nfulfils its duties under section 8; and\n(b) include a forecast of the revenue and expenditure of the\nCorporation and its subsidiaries, including a forecast of\ncapital expenditure and borrowings; and\n(c) include such other matters as are prescribed in the regulations\nmade for the purposes of this Act.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-31b"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-31b-ss-1-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-31b-ss-1-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "8286d87e1d39931996203e672a1c5e50c1bc738b91d9d603891d4b0926a361cd",
      "skos:note": "Corporate plan must outline strategies and policies, forecast revenue and expenditure, and include other prescribed matters.",
      "dc:description": "Yes"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983#sec-31b-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "31B(1) Matters to be included in corporate plans",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 54,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Each corporate plan prepared by the Board under section 35 of the\nPublic Governance, Performance and Accountability Act 2013\nmust:\n(a) outline the overall strategies and policies that the Corporation\nand its subsidiaries are to follow to ensure that the Board\nfulfils its duties under section 8; and\n(b) include a forecast of the revenue and expenditure of the\nCorporation and its subsidiaries, including a forecast of\ncapital expenditure and borrowings; and\n(c) include such other matters as are prescribed in the regulations\nmade for the purposes of this Act."
    },
