    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-68",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "68 Application of money",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983#sec-68"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983.pdf, p.57",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The money of the Corporation shall be applied only:\n(a) in payment or discharge of the expenses, charges, obligations\nor liabilities incurred or undertaken by the Corporation in or\nin connection with the performance of its functions or the\nexercise of its powers;\n(b) in payment of any remuneration or allowances payable under\nthis Act (other than Part IIIA); and\n(c) in making any other payments that are required by this Act to\nbe made out of the moneys of the Corporation.\n(2) Subsection (1) does not prevent investment, under section 59 of the\nPublic Governance, Performance and Accountability Act 2013, of\nmoney that is not immediately required for the purposes of the\nCorporation.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The money of the Corporation shall be applied only:\n(a) in payment or discharge of the expenses, charges, obligations\nor liabilities incurred or undertaken by the Corporation in or\nin connection with the performance of its functions or the\nexercise of its powers;\n(b) in payment of any remuneration or allowances payable under\nthis Act (other than Part IIIA); and\n(c) in making any other payments that are required by this Act to\nbe made out of the moneys of the Corporation.\n(2) Subsection (1) does not prevent investment, under section 59 of the\nPublic Governance, Performance and Accountability Act 2013, of\nmoney that is not immediately required for the purposes of the\nCorporation.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-68-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-68-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "80ec04992ebc82aab5764987e0123ba8ef33bbe9573016449eec6dc9d02dca51"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983#sec-68",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "68 Application of money",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 57,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The money of the Corporation shall be applied only:\n(a) in payment or discharge of the expenses, charges, obligations\nor liabilities incurred or undertaken by the Corporation in or\nin connection with the performance of its functions or the\nexercise of its powers;\n(b) in payment of any remuneration or allowances payable under\nthis Act (other than Part IIIA); and\n(c) in making any other payments that are required by this Act to\nbe made out of the moneys of the Corporation.\n(2) Subsection (1) does not prevent investment, under section 59 of the\nPublic Governance, Performance and Accountability Act 2013, of\nmoney that is not immediately required for the purposes of the\nCorporation."
    },
