      "skos:definition": "(1) If the Minister is of the opinion that the broadcasting of particular\nmatter by the Corporation would be in the national interest, the\nMinister may direct the Corporation to broadcast that matter over\nall of its national broadcasting services or over such of them as are\nspecified in the direction. If such a direction is given, the\nCorporation must broadcast that matter, free of charge, in\naccordance with the direction.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-78"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-78-ss-1-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-78-ss-1-logic-deontic-1"
