      "cml:integrityHash": "cc027ab35060104213631aa05eeb32fc57b9a1a5056ef1a720c89e4c9d28d696",
      "skos:note": "Minister may direct Corporation to broadcast matter over national broadcasting services.",
      "dc:description": "Free of charge"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983#sec-78-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "78(1) Power of Minister to give directions to Corporation in the",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 62,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If the Minister is of the opinion that the broadcasting of particular\nmatter by the Corporation would be in the national interest, the\nMinister may direct the Corporation to broadcast that matter over\nall of its national broadcasting services or over such of them as are\nspecified in the direction. If such a direction is given, the\nCorporation must broadcast that matter, free of charge, in\naccordance with the direction."
    },
