    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-78-ss-3a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "78(3A) Power of Minister to give directions to Corporation in the",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983#sec-78-ss-3a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983.pdf, p.62",
      "values:originalText": "(3A) If the Minister is of the opinion that the provision of particular\ncontent by the Corporation would be in the national interest, the\nMinister may direct the Corporation to provide that content on all\nof its digital media services or on such of them as are specified in\nthe direction. If such a direction is given, the Corporation must\nprovide that content, free of charge, in accordance with the\ndirection.",
      "skos:definition": "(3A) If the Minister is of the opinion that the provision of particular\ncontent by the Corporation would be in the national interest, the\nMinister may direct the Corporation to provide that content on all\nof its digital media services or on such of them as are specified in\nthe direction. If such a direction is given, the Corporation must\nprovide that content, free of charge, in accordance with the\ndirection.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-78"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-78-ss-3a-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-78-ss-3a-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "56615f7565b9610e1a6edadb923d1284a4f93d32ccd4afd0eebb81c49edadc0e",
      "skos:note": "Minister may direct Corporation to provide content on digital media services.",
      "dc:description": "true"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983#sec-78-ss-3a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "78(3A) Power of Minister to give directions to Corporation in the",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 62,
      "values:originalText": "(3A) If the Minister is of the opinion that the provision of particular\ncontent by the Corporation would be in the national interest, the\nMinister may direct the Corporation to provide that content on all\nof its digital media services or on such of them as are specified in\nthe direction. If such a direction is given, the Corporation must\nprovide that content, free of charge, in accordance with the\ndirection."
    },
